# Pub/Sub (B-27): confirmations, delivery to channel and pattern subscribers, and the subscribe mode.
# Several connections: `@sub`, `@psub` and `@both` subscribe; the unnamed one publishes. A mass
# unsubscribe answers in the order of Redis's dictionary, and each confirmation carries the count left,
# so it is compared only where its order is determined: with one subscription left, and with none.
FLUSHALL
PUBLISH nobody hi
SUBSCRIBE
PUBLISH only-channel
@sub SUBSCRIBE news
[frames 2] @sub SUBSCRIBE a b
@sub SUBSCRIBE news
PUBLISH news hello
[read 1] @sub
@psub PSUBSCRIBE app:*
[frames 2] @psub PSUBSCRIBE n?ws x
PUBLISH news again
[read 1] @sub
[read 1] @psub
PUBLISH app:home:42 "hello there"
[read 1] @psub
PUBLISH "binary\x00channel" "\xff\x00"
# A client on a channel and on a pattern that matches it receives the message twice: the channel first.
@both SUBSCRIBE t
@both PSUBSCRIBE t*
PUBLISH t x
[read 2] @both
# In subscribe mode only (un)subscribing, PING and QUIT are served.
@sub GET k
@sub SET k v
@sub CLIENT LIST
@sub PING
@sub PING hi
@sub UNSUBSCRIBE news
PUBLISH news gone
@sub UNSUBSCRIBE a
@sub UNSUBSCRIBE
@sub UNSUBSCRIBE
@sub GET k
@sub PUNSUBSCRIBE
@sub PING
[frames 2] @psub PUNSUBSCRIBE app:* n?ws
@psub PUNSUBSCRIBE
@psub UNSUBSCRIBE nothere
@psub PSUBSCRIBE "[ab]*"
PUBLISH b1 m
[read 1] @psub
[closes] @both QUIT
FLUSHALL
